READING.
  'Admissible' = the cascade actually produces it (owner, 2026-09-18). This run counts ONLY
  cascades that ARRIVE, so every configuration below is one the determinator reaches from
  the bound and then terminates on.

  delta is driven from 4.98e-07 to 6.10e-13 through refinement scales well above double
  precision, then to machine epsilon. No floor appears at any scale.

  So c_* > 0 is REFUTED. To survive, the lemma would need c_* <= 6.10e-13 -- and a
  'universal constant' of that size is vacuous: it bounds the move a returning setter forces
  by nothing usable. The infimum is 0 and is not attained.

  HONEST LIMIT: the last two rows (5.99e-15, 2.22e-16) sit at or below double precision and
  should not be trusted. The refutation rests on 6.10e-13, which is three orders clear of
  the floor and reached by a cascade that arrives in finitely many moves.

  WHAT SURVIVES: the extremality. inf over g >= 4 equalled inf over g = 4 in 20,000 random
  arrangements, and the pushed counterexample is also a g = 4 return. More intervening moves
  did not produce a shallower setter. That half of the lemma is untouched by this.
